<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eildon Hills</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eildon Hills are a group of three volcanic summits above Melrose in the Scottish Borders. Their triple peak gave its name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trimontium">Trimontium</a>, the Roman fort built beneath them at Newstead. The hills are also rich in legend, linked with Thomas the Rhymer and tales of King Arthur.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eildon-hills.jpg" alt="Eildon Hills" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jenny Gumbrell · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eildon_Village_-_geograph.org.uk_-_55018.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
